<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ajmer-Merwara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1818–1950</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Ajmer-Merwara Province</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ajmer-Merwara was a small province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-india">British India</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputana">Rajputana</a>, formed from the district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajmer">Ajmer</a>, ceded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> to the British in 1818, and the hill tract of Merwara. Ruled directly by a chief commissioner among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a>, it became the Part C state of Ajmer in 1950 and was merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a> under the States Reorganisation Act in 1956.</p></div>
